@page "/behind-the-build"
@using FactoryPulse.Web.Content

<PageTitle>Behind the Build | FactoryPulse</PageTitle>

<div class="build-page">
    <nav class="build-nav" aria-label="Case study navigation">
        <a class="brand-lockup" href="/">
            <span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true">FP</span>
            <span><strong>FactoryPulse</strong><small>Engineering case study</small></span>
        </a>
        <div class="nav-actions">
            <a class="text-link" href="@BehindTheBuildContent.RepositoryUrl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
            <a class="dashboard-link" href="/">Open dashboard <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
    </nav>

    <main>
        <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
            <div class="hero-copy">
                <p class="kicker"><span></span> Build record · @BehindTheBuildContent.SnapshotDate</p>
                <h1 id="page-title">Behind the <em>Build</em></h1>
                <p class="hero-subtitle">AI-Assisted Development. Human-Directed Engineering.</p>
                <p class="hero-intro">
                    FactoryPulse is an industrial monitoring demonstration built through a milestone-driven,
                    AI-assisted workflow. Codex contributed heavily to implementation; the problem definition,
                    requirements, architecture choices, reviews, validation, and responsibility for the result
                    remained human-led.
                </p>
                <div class="hero-actions">
                    <a class="primary-action" href="/">Explore the live dashboard <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
                    <a class="secondary-action" href="@BehindTheBuildContent.RepositoryUrl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Review the source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
                </div>
            </div>

            <aside class="hero-console" aria-label="Project engineering summary">
                <div class="console-bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><small>build-profile.json</small></div>
                <dl>
                    <div><dt>domain</dt><dd>industrial monitoring</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>delivery</dt><dd>6 verified milestones</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>validation</dt><dd class="signal-good">32 tests passing</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>telemetry</dt><dd>OPC UA · encrypted</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>persistence</dt><dd>SQLite · observable</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>ownership</dt><dd class="signal-human">human directed</dd></div>
                </dl>
                <p><span class="pulse" aria-hidden="true"></span> Repository-backed facts only</p>
            </aside>
        </section>

        <section class="section-block stats-section" aria-labelledby="statistics-heading">
            <div class="section-heading">
                <div>
                    <p class="section-index">01 / Evidence</p>
                    <h2 id="statistics-heading">Development statistics</h2>
                </div>
                <p>Measured facts are separated from unknowns. Expand any card to inspect its methodology.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="stats-grid">
                @foreach (var metric in BehindTheBuildContent.ProjectMetrics)
                {
                    <article class="stat-card @(metric.IsMeasured ? "is-measured" : "is-unknown")">
                        <div class="stat-topline">
                            <span>@metric.Label</span>
                            <span class="metric-status">@metric.Status</span>
                        </div>
                        <strong>@metric.Value</strong>
                        <details class="metric-method">
                            <summary>How this is sourced</summary>
                            <p>@metric.Methodology</p>
                        </details>
                    </article>
                }
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section-block workflow-section" aria-labelledby="workflow-heading">
            <div class="section-heading">
                <div>
                    <p class="section-index">02 / Process</p>
                    <h2 id="workflow-heading">A directed AI workflow</h2>
                </div>
                <p>AI accelerated implementation inside an engineering loop—not outside one.</p>
            </div>

            <ol class="workflow-track">
                @foreach (var stage in BehindTheBuildContent.Workflow)
                {
                    <li>
                        <span class="stage-number">@stage.Number</span>
                        <h3>@stage.Title</h3>
                        <p>@stage.Description</p>
                    </li>
                }
            </ol>
        </section>

        <section class="section-block timeline-section" aria-labelledby="timeline-heading">
            <div class="section-heading">
                <div>
                    <p class="section-index">03 / Delivery</p>
                    <h2 id="timeline-heading">Built incrementally</h2>
                </div>
                <p>Each milestone added one layer of industrial behavior while keeping the application runnable.</p>
            </div>

            <ol class="timeline-list">
                @foreach (var milestone in BehindTheBuildContent.Milestones)
                {
                    <li>
                        <span class="timeline-marker" aria-hidden="true">@milestone.Number.ToString("00")</span>
                        <details class="timeline-card" open="@(milestone.Number == 1)">
                            <summary>
                                <span>
                                    <small>Milestone @milestone.Number · <time datetime="@milestone.CompletedOn.ToString("yyyy-MM-dd")">@milestone.CompletedOn.ToString("MMM d, yyyy")</time></small>
                                    <strong>@milestone.Title</strong>
                                </span>
                                <span class="expand-label"><span class="when-closed">Expand</span><span class="when-open">Collapse</span></span>
                            </summary>
                            <div class="timeline-detail">
                                <p>@milestone.Description</p>
                                <div class="concept-list" aria-label="Technologies and concepts">
                                    @foreach (var concept in milestone.Concepts)
                                    {
                                        <span>@concept</span>
                                    }
                                </div>
                                <a href="@milestone.CommitUrl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View commit @milestone.Commit <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
                            </div>
                        </details>
                    </li>
                }
            </ol>
        </section>

        <section class="section-block challenges-section" aria-labelledby="challenges-heading">
            <div class="section-heading">
                <div>
                    <p class="section-index">04 / Judgment</p>
                    <h2 id="challenges-heading">Where review changed the result</h2>
                </div>
                <p>The strongest evidence of engineering is not first-pass output—it is finding what could fail and correcting it.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="challenge-grid">
                @foreach (var challenge in BehindTheBuildContent.Challenges)
                {
                    <article class="challenge-card">
                        <header>
                            <span class="challenge-icon" aria-hidden="true">!</span>
                            <h3>@challenge.Title</h3>
                        </header>
                        <dl>
                            <div><dt>What surfaced</dt><dd>@challenge.Problem</dd></div>
                            <div><dt>Why it mattered</dt><dd>@challenge.Impact</dd></div>
                            <div class="resolution"><dt>Engineering response</dt><dd>@challenge.Resolution</dd></div>
                        </dl>
                        <a href="@challenge.CommitUrl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Evidence: @challenge.Commit <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
                    </article>
                }
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section-block stack-section" aria-labelledby="stack-heading">
            <div class="section-heading">
                <div>
                    <p class="section-index">05 / System</p>
                    <h2 id="stack-heading">Technology with a job to do</h2>
                </div>
                <p>No ornamental dependencies. Each item below has a verified role in the repository.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="stack-grid">
                @foreach (var technology in BehindTheBuildContent.Technologies)
                {
                    <article>
                        <span class="stack-node" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        <h3>@technology.Name</h3>
                        <p>@technology.Role</p>
                    </article>
                }
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section-block usage-section" aria-labelledby="usage-heading">
            <div class="section-heading">
                <div>
                    <p class="section-index">06 / Transparency</p>
                    <h2 id="usage-heading">AI usage, without invented precision</h2>
                </div>
                <p>The interface is ready for audited project metrics later. Unknown values remain visibly unknown today.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="usage-layout">
                <div class="usage-table" role="list" aria-label="AI usage metrics">
                    @foreach (var metric in BehindTheBuildContent.AiUsageMetrics)
                    {
                        <div role="listitem">
                            <span>@metric.Label</span>
                            <strong class="@(metric.IsMeasured ? null : "unknown-value")">@metric.Value</strong>
                            <p>@metric.Methodology</p>
                        </div>
                    }
                </div>
                <aside class="data-guardrail">
                    <p class="section-index">Data guardrail</p>
                    <h3>What is deliberately not claimed</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Commit timestamps are not converted into human hours.</li>
                        <li>Source-code size is not converted into token usage.</li>
                        <li>Subscription access is not presented as API billing.</li>
                        <li>No private transcripts, credentials, or raw session logs are published.</li>
                        <li>No speedup is stated without a recorded comparison baseline.</li>
                    </ul>
                </aside>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section-block value-section" aria-labelledby="value-heading">
            <div class="value-copy">
                <p class="section-index">07 / Value</p>
                <h2 id="value-heading">Why the workflow matters</h2>
                <p>
                    AI assistance can shorten repetitive implementation cycles, accelerate prototypes, generate test
                    scaffolding, and make unfamiliar protocols faster to explore. For a small engineering team, that can
                    mean more capacity for integration, validation, and operator-focused refinement.
                </p>
                <p>
                    The benefit is conditional: complex domain rules, security decisions, time-bound calculations, and
                    failure handling still demand careful review. FactoryPulse treats speed as useful only when the result
                    remains understandable, testable, and honest about its limits.
                </p>
            </div>
            <blockquote>
                <span aria-hidden="true">“</span>
                <p>AI accelerates implementation. Engineering judgment determines whether the result is reliable.</p>
                <footer>FactoryPulse engineering principle</footer>
            </blockquote>
        </section>

        <section class="engineering-commitment" aria-labelledby="commitment-heading">
            <p class="section-index">Professional responsibility</p>
            <h2 id="commitment-heading">Understand it. Challenge it. Own it.</h2>
            <p>
                Generated code is still delivered code. That means maintaining clear requirements, understanding the
                implementation, validating assumptions, testing edge cases, reviewing security and reliability, and
                taking responsibility for every behavior exposed to an operator.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="final-cta" aria-labelledby="cta-heading">
            <div>
                <p class="section-index">Continue exploring</p>
                <h2 id="cta-heading">See the engineering in motion.</h2>
                <p>Operate the simulator, inspect the telemetry, and review the source behind each decision.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="cta-actions">
                <a class="primary-action" href="/">Launch the dashboard <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
                <a class="secondary-action" href="@BehindTheBuildContent.RepositoryUrl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Browse GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
            </div>
        </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="build-footer">
        <span>FactoryPulse · Industrial software portfolio project</span>
        <a href="#page-title">Back to top ↑</a>
    </footer>
</div>
